<title>UK: RESEARCH ALERT - Lehman picks Euro stocks for 1997.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Lehman picks Euro stocks for 1997.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Strategists at Lehman Brothers on Wednesday named eight continental European stocks they expect to outperform through 1997, as part of a pan-European list of 19 stocks they favour for the year.  </p>
<p>In continental Europe they picked French insurance group Axa, Finnish mobile phone maker Nokia Oy, Germany's Volkswagen AG, French foods group Groupe Danone SA, French financial group Compagnie Bancaire SA, Italian oil group ENI SpA, Swiss elevator manufacturer Schindler Holding AG and Swedish banking group Nordbanken.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
</text>
